+/*
+ * Faber peripherals for the ESP32 family (ESP32, ESP32-S3, ESP32-C3): register-level models of
+ * the blocks QEMU does not model (or only stubs), whose activity crosses the Faber bridge as
+ * time-stamped events (hw/gpio/esp32_gpio.c documents the line protocol):
+ *
+ *   LEDC     PWM channels: frequency, duty and phase per channel ("L"), hardware fades, interrupts
+ *   GP-SPI   SPI2 / SPI3 masters in CPU mode (W0..W15 buffer): one "SX" per transaction, timed by
+ *            the configured SPI clock; MISO is fetched from Faber ("SQ") only when the firmware
+ *            reads the buffer back
+ *   RMT      TX channels: symbols from channel RAM ("RM"), ping-pong refill (threshold interrupt),
+ *            wrap mode, end marker, timed by the RMT clock
+ *   ADC      oneshot conversions (ESP32 / S3: SENS SAR1/SAR2; C3: APB_SARADC) from the pad voltage
+ *            Faber sets ("E"), with each chip's attenuation ranges
+ *   I2S      standard (Philips) TX/RX through DMA (ESP32: I2S DMA lldesc lists; S3/C3: GDMA): frames
+ *            out as "ST", frames in from "SR" queries
+ *   I2C      ESP32-S3 / C3 controllers (the ESP32's controller with the newer command opcodes)
+ *
+ * Fidelity notes live in Faber (docs/esp32-peripherals.md).
+ *
+ * This program is free software; you can redistribute it and/or modify it under the terms of the
+ * GNU General Public License version 2 or (at your option) any later version.
+ */
+
